---
import Layout from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Support — MyBodyPrism"
  description="Get help with MyBodyPrism. Contact us at support@mybodyprism.com."
>
  <section class="container narrow">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:support@mybodyprism.com">support@mybodyprism.com</a>.
      We answer within one business day. For urgent issues mention "urgent" in
      the subject line.
    </p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>How do I install the Desktop Viewer?</summary>
      <p>
        Download the installer from the <a href="/pricing">download page</a>
        (the download starts right in your browser). Run it; on first launch the
        viewer activates a <strong>free license</strong> automatically — no code
        needed.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What are the system requirements?</summary>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/system-requirements">system requirements page</a>.
        Short version: Windows 10/11, an NVIDIA RTX 2060 or better, 16 GB
        RAM, 5 GB free disk.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does it cost anything?</summary>
      <p>
        No — MyBodyPrism is <strong>free</strong> in this version. There's no
        charge, so there's nothing to buy or refund. See the
        <a href="/legal/tos">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Is it really free? Will it stay free?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes, it's free in this version, with no time limit. We can't promise
        it will be free forever: we may introduce paid features in the future
        and would give registered users notice first. Browser-based streaming,
        when it arrives, will be a paid feature.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>I moved to a new computer — how do I get my license there?</summary>
      <p>
        The free license is issued per machine. On a new machine, just
        download and launch again to get a fresh free license. Reinstalling on
        the same machine keeps your existing license. Any trouble — write to
        support.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does my imaging leave my machine?</summary>
      <p>
        No. MyBodyPrism is a desktop viewer that runs entirely on your
        machine, with no upload and no AI processing — your DICOM files never
        leave your computer. The only network calls it makes are to activate
        and verify your license. See the
        <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why does Windows SmartScreen warn me about the installer?</summary>
      <p>
        New code-signing certificates can take a few weeks to build
        reputation with Microsoft SmartScreen. If you see a warning, click
        "More info" → "Run anyway". The installer is digitally signed by
        MyBodyPrism; we'll have full SmartScreen reputation soon.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>I forgot my account email or lost access to it.</summary>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:support@mybodyprism.com">support</a> from
        whatever address you have, with as much purchase detail as you can
        provide (approximate date, last four of the card you used). We'll
        verify and migrate your account.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Is MyBodyPrism HIPAA-compliant?</summary>
      <p>
        In this version your DICOM data stays on your device, so there is no
        PHI for us to hold and HIPAA does not apply to us in that relationship.
        See our <a href="/legal/hipaa">HIPAA notice</a>.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <style>
    .narrow { max-width: 760px; padding: 2rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
    details {
      border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      background: var(--c-panel);
    }
    summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
    details[open] summary { color: var(--c-brand); }
  </style>
</Layout>
